# Common mistakes with each aggregate: a wrong argument type (DS2006) or count (DS2002). Each is
# reported on its own.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
| summarize
    countif(amount),
    sum(customerId),
    sumif(amount, customerId),
    avg(amount > 1),
    min(),
    max(amount, 2),
    dcount(),
    percentile(amount),
    stdev(customerId),
    variance(timestamp),
    take_any(),
    count(amount)
---- expected
error[DS2006]: argument `predicate` of `countif` must be `bool`, found `real`
  --> query:3:13
  |
3 |     countif(amount),
  |             ^^^^^^ this is `real` (column `amount` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: to test whether it is not zero, compare it: `amount != 0`
  = note: signature: `countif(predicate: bool) -> long`

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `sum` must be a number or `timespan`, found `string`
  --> query:4:9
  |
4 |     sum(customerId),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = note: `sum` has these forms: `sum(x: T) -> long or real`, where T is a number; `sum(x: timespan) -> timespan`

error[DS2006]: argument `predicate` of `sumif` must be `bool`, found `string`
  --> query:5:19
  |
5 |     sumif(amount, customerId),
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `tobool(customerId)`
  = note: `sumif` has these forms: `sumif(x: T, predicate: bool) -> long or real`, where T is a number; `sumif(x: timespan, predicate: bool) -> timespan`

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `avg` must be a number or `timespan`, found `bool`
  --> query:6:9
  |
6 |     avg(amount > 1),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `bool`
  |
  = note: `avg` has these forms: `avg(x: number) -> real`; `avg(x: timespan) -> timespan`

error[DS2002]: `min` takes 1 argument, found 0
  --> query:7:5
  |
7 |     min(),
  |     ^^^^^ missing `x`
  |
  = note: signature: `min(x: T) -> T`, where T is a number, `string`, `datetime`, `timespan` or `bool`

error[DS2002]: `max` takes 1 argument, found 2
  --> query:8:17
  |
8 |     max(amount, 2),
  |                 ^ this argument is not expected
  |
  = note: signature: `max(x: T) -> T`, where T is a number, `string`, `datetime`, `timespan` or `bool`

error[DS2002]: `dcount` takes 1 argument, found 0
  --> query:9:5
  |
9 |     dcount(),
  |     ^^^^^^^^ missing `x`
  |
  = note: signature: `dcount(x: any) -> long`

error[DS2002]: `percentile` takes 2 arguments, found 1
   --> query:10:5
   |
10 |     percentile(amount),
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ missing `percentage`
   |
   = note: `percentile` has these forms: `percentile(x: T, percentage: number) -> T`, where T is a number; `percentile(x: datetime, percentage: number) -> datetime`; `percentile(x: timespan, percentage: number) -> timespan`

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `stdev` must be a number, found `string`
   --> query:11:11
   |
11 |     stdev(customerId),
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
   |
   = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `toreal(customerId)`
   = note: signature: `stdev(x: number) -> real`

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `variance` must be a number, found `datetime`
   --> query:12:14
   |
12 |     variance(timestamp),
   |              ^^^^^^^^^ this is `datetime` (column `timestamp` was read from orders.csv)
   |
   = note: signature: `variance(x: number) -> real`

error[DS2002]: `take_any` takes 1 argument, found 0
   --> query:13:5
   |
13 |     take_any(),
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^ missing `x`
   |
   = note: signature: `take_any(x: T) -> T`

error[DS2002]: `count` takes no arguments, found 1
   --> query:14:11
   |
14 |     count(amount)
   |           ^^^^^^ this argument is not expected
   |
   = help: `count()` counts rows; to count the rows where `amount` is not null, use `countif(isnotnull(amount))`
   = note: signature: `count() -> long`
